tic scientific demonstration. The scene only contains the described setup and actions. The green kinetic sand is located on a wooden table, and the blue-black grabber tool is suspended over it. The blue-black grabber tool releases the blue tennis ball above a pile of green kinetic sand.\n\n---RULES---\n# PixelWorld generation contract v2\n\n- Use only `first_frame.png`, `prompt.txt` and `task_spec.json`. Work inside this workspace. No network, other cases, reference continuations, masks, scores, memory, external AI models, learned weights, external simulation/rendering engines, or subagents.\n- Generate 120 RGB frames at 512×288, 24 fps, for 5 seconds. Frame 00 must be pixel-identical to `first_frame.png`.\n- You must create `generate.py`, run it, and call `artifact_io.save(frames, case_dir)` at least once before finishing. Finish only after the required output artifacts exist. Keep `generate.py` runnable so it regenerates the submitted RGB video.\n- Local Python/numpy/PIL, mathematical geometry, motion, lighting, copying and warping pixels are allowed.\n- If you revise the video, save each revised candidate before continuing. Avoid repeated revision without a clear expected improvement; aim for high-quality output while considering efficiency.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"},{"kind":"agent_message","utc":"2026-11-13T13:31:16.248756+00:00","text":"Iâll analyze the first frame numerically, then animate the grabber releasing the ball and the ball settling into the sand while keeping the camera fixed."},{"kind":"command_execution","utc":"2026-11-13T13:31:17.840441+00:00","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat task_spec.json && cat artifact_io.py && python - <<'PY'\nfrom PIL import Image\nimport numpy as np\nim=np.array(Image.open('first_frame.png').convert('RGB'))\nprint('shape',im.shape)\nfor y in range(0,288,8):\n s=''\n for x in range(0,512,8):\n  r,g,b=np.median(im[y:y+8,x:x+8].reshape(-1,3),axis=0)\n  if g>r*1.25 and g>b*1.15: c='G'\n  elif b>r*1.15 and b>g*1.03: c='B'\n  elif max(r,g,b)<60:c='#'\n  elif max(r,g,b)<110:c='o'\n  elif r>g*1.12 and r>b*1.18: c='w'\n  elif min(r,g,b)>190: c='.'\n  else: c='-'\n  s+=c\n print(f'{y:3} {s}')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"task_type\": \"i2v\",\n  \"width\": 512,\n  \"height\": 288,\n  \"frames\": 120,\n  \"fps\": 24,\n  \"audio\": null,\n  \"benchmark\": \"physics_iq_highres_24fps\"\n}\n\"\"\"Output-only helpers. No drawing or generation policy is implemented here.\"\"\"\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport base64\nimport json\nimport wave\n\nimport numpy as np\nfrom PIL import Image, ImageDraw\n\n\ndef save(frames, case_dir, audio=None):\n    case_dir = Path(case_dir)\n    frames = np.asarray(frames)\n    path = case_dir / \"task_spec.json\"\n    spec = json.loads(path.read_text()) if path.is_file() else {}\n    n, h, w, fps = (spec.get(\"frames\", 20), spec.get(\"height\", 144), spec.get(\"width\", 256), spec.get(\"fps\", 4))\n    assert frames.shape == (n, h, w, 3) and frames.dtype == np.uint8, frames.shape\n    audio_spec = spec.get(\"audio\")\n    audio_url = None\n    if audio_spec:\n        samples = round(n / fps * audio_spec[\"sample_rate\"])\n        pcm = np.asarray(audio)\n        if pcm.ndim == 1:\n            pcm = pcm[:, None]\n        assert pcm.shape == (samples, audio_spec[\"channels\"]) and pcm.dtype == np.int16, (pcm.shape, pcm.dtype)\n        with wave.open(str(case_dir / \"audio.wav\"), \"wb\") as handle:\n            handle.setnchannels(audio_spec[\"channels\"])\n            handle.setsampwidth(2)\n            handle.setframerate(audio_spec[\"sample_rate\"])\n            handle.writeframes(pcm.astype(\"<i2\").tobytes())\n        audio_url = \"data:audio/wav;base64,\" + base64.b64encode((case_dir / \"audio.wav\").read_bytes()).decode()\n    values = frames.astype(np.uint32)\n    packed = (values[:, :, :, 0] << 16) | (values[:, :, :, 1] << 8) | values[:, :, :, 2]\n    tensor = packed.transpose(1, 2, 0)\n    np.savez_compressed(case_dir / \"pixels.npz\", pixels=tensor)\n\n    folder = case_dir / \"frames\"\n    folder.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n    for index, frame in enumerate(frames):\n        Image.fromarray(frame).save(folder / f\"{index:02d}.png\")\n\n    sheet = Image.new(\"RGB\", (w * 4, (h + 21) * 2), (25, 28, 35))\n    draw = ImageDraw.Draw(sheet)\n    for index, frame_index in enumerate(np.linspace(0, n - 1, 8).round().astype(int)):\n        x, y = (index % 4) * w, (index // 4) * (h + 21)\n        draw.text((x + 5, y + 3), f\"frame {frame_index:02d} · {frame_index / fps:.2f}s\", fill=\"white\")\n        sheet.paste(Image.fromarray(frames[frame_index]), (x, y + 21))\n    sheet.save(case_dir / \"inspection.png\")\n\n    transition = Image.new(\"RGB\", (w * 4, h * 2 + 21), (25, 28, 35))\n    draw = ImageDraw.Draw(transition)\n    for index, frame_index in enumerate(min(i, n-1) for i in range(4)):\n        x = index * w\n        draw.text((x + 5, 4), f\"frame {frame_index:02d} · {frame_index / fps:.2f}s\", fill=\"white\")\n        transition.paste(Image.fromarray(frames[frame_index]), (x, 21))\n        transition.paste(Image.fromarray(frames[frame_index]).resize((w, h), Image.Resampling.NEAREST), (x, h + 21))\n    transition.save(case_dir / \"transition_check.png\")\n\n    encode = lambda array: base64.b64encode(np.asarray(array, dtype=\"<u4\").tobytes()).decode()\n    deltas = []\n    for index in range(1, n):\n        current = packed[index].reshape(-1)\n        previous = packed[index - 1].reshape(-1)\n        positions = np.flatnonzero(current != previous)\n        packet = []\n        if len(positions):\n            bounds = np.r_[0, np.flatnonzero(np.diff(positions) > 1) + 1, len(positions)]\n            for start, end in zip(bounds[:-1], bounds[1:]):\n                offset = int(positions[start])\n                count = int(end - start)\n                packet.extend([offset, count])\n                packet.extend(current[offset:offset + count].tolist())\n        deltas.append(encode(packet))\n    data = {\n        \"id\": case_dir.name,\n        \"width\": w, \"height\": h, \"frames\": n, \"fps\": fps, \"audio\": audio_url,\n        \"first\": encode(packed[0].reshape(-1)),\n        \"deltas\": deltas,\n        \"caption\": (case_dir / \"prompt.txt\").read_text().strip(),\n    }\n    template = (Path(__file__).parent / \"player_template.html\").read_text()\n    payload = json.dumps(data, separators=(\",\", \":\"), ensure_ascii=False).replace(\"<\", \"\\\\u003c\")\n    (case_dir / \"index.html\").write_text(template.replace(\"__ID__\", case_dir.name).replace(\"__DATA__\", payload))\nshape (288, 512, 3)\n  0 ----------------------------#BBBBBBBB---------------------------\n  8 ---------------------------#BBBBBBBBBB--------------------------\n 16 ---------------------------BBB-----BBB--------------------------\n 24 ---------------------------BB-------BB--------------------------\n 32 ---------------------------BB--------BB-------------------------\n 40 ---------------------------BB--------BB-------------------------\n 48 ---------------------------oB---BBBB-BB-------------------------\n 56 ----------------------------B--BBBBBB---------------------------\n 64 ----------------------------BBBBBBBBBB--------------------------\n 72 ------------------------------BBBBBBBB--------------------------\n 80 ------------------------------BBBBBBBB--------------------------\n 88 ------------------------------BBBBBBBB--------------------------\n 96 -------------------------------BBBBBB---------------------------\n104 --------------------------------BBBB----------------------------\n112 ----------------------------------------------------------------\n120 -------------------------------------------------wwwwwww-------o\n128 o-----------------------------------------wwwwwwwwwwwwwwww-oo-oo\n136 oo---------------------------------wwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwooo\n144 ooo-------------------------wwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwo\n152 ooooo----------------wwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwww